{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>YHWH</b> — the accent [te'am] of 'day' — [it is] a temporal expression, like אתה עובר היום (you pass through today), היום הזה יום בשורה הוא (this day is a day of tidings), ביום הכותי כל בכור (on the day I struck every firstborn)." "<b>and the day of my cry</b> — connected with what comes after it."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 88, :notes {0 "The comment addresses the word ה' (YHWH) and apparently explains that the accent mark on 'יום' in verse 2 indicates a temporal sense, supporting this with three biblical parallels."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:36:16.851205229Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}